{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## SECOND repo-wide CI blocker found: scanner-integration fails on every change since it merged\n\nFiled 90c7-c465-4037-42d5 / floppy-patriotic-unau, priority 0, agent dispatched.\n\nTWO INDEPENDENT GATES ARE NOW FAILING REPO-WIDE SIMULTANEOUSLY and no change can reach Verified +1.\nSix open changes blocked: 2594, 2600, 2601, 2607, 2608, 2609.\n\nThe board reads five changes at LLM+1 / Verified-1, which initially looked like one problem (9a17).\nIt is two. Comparing the FAILING JOB LISTS rather than the vote states separated them:\n  2594: pytest py3.13 only                        -> 9a17\n  2601: pytest py3.13 + py3.12 + scanner-integration\n  2607: pytest py3.11 + py3.13 + scanner-integration\n  2608: scanner-integration ONLY, no pytest failures\n2608 is the decisive case: its only failing job is scanner-integration, so that job fails\nINDEPENDENTLY OF CHANGE CONTENT. Several changes failing both is what masked it. Lesson for the loop:\ncompare failing JOB LISTS across changes, not vote states -- identical -1s can be different defects,\nand one clean isolate is worth more than four ambiguous ones.\n\nORIGIN: .github/workflows/_scanner-integration.yml arrived in 6125c5345f01 ('Pin review scanner\ncontracts in Verified', change 2595), merged 03:37:02 with LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1. It passed\nits own CI and then broke everyone else's.\n\nTHIRD INSTANCE TODAY OF TRUSTED-MAIN ASYMMETRY, and the first that actually LANDED:\n 1. 2600 patchset 1 added an unguarded 'make e2e-deps' that, run from trusted main against a base\n    predating the rule, would have failed the install step on every other open change. CAUGHT\n    pre-merge by tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py.\n 2. 2600 patchset 2 drew LLM-Review -1 for the same class: 'npm ci && npm run build' with no failure\n    tolerance hard-failing the install step on a transient npm fault. Caught in review.\n 3. This one -- NOT caught, and merged.\nThe mechanism is structural: the Verified lane runs workflows from TRUSTED MAIN against an arbitrary\npatchset, so a new CI job is validated under conditions that do not match how it will subsequently\nrun. When 2595 was tested, main did not yet carry the workflow, so 2595 could not have exercised it\nthe way main now does. That is why AC3 on the new ticket is about closing the PRE-MERGE detection\ngap, not just repairing this job -- the same shape will land again otherwise.\n\nStale base explicitly ruled out as sufficient: change 2607 was branched from 6125c5345f01 ITSELF --\nthe very commit that added the workflow -- and still fails. The agent was told not to stop at that\nhypothesis.\n\nAlso told it not to unilaterally revert another session's merged work: if the right answer turns out\nto be reverting or disabling the job rather than repairing it, stop and escalate for a decision.\n\nBoard: 9 orphan bugs (2 open, 7 in_progress). 2609 (S6) is LLM+1 with CI still running -- if it comes\nback green on scanner-integration that would be informative, since it was pushed from a later base."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788498720051201001,"uuid":"eebe0056-4acb-4baf-9b4b-0fd9ed1fe59b"}